NEW RUST TESTS (5 turn + 2 store + 1 retrieve, all named *_f07)
  turn::query_scoped_ledger_serves_a_repeat_its_own_answer_f07
      13000-char passages so the per-ref budget serves EXACTLY ONE, which makes
      "which passage the model actually sees" the observable:
        turn 1        -> f07zero, ledger conv_a = [0]
        same Q again  -> f07zero (the F07 defect: it used to lose its own answer)
        "show me other passages ..." -> f07one, ledger = [0,1]
        other conversation conv_b    -> f07zero, own ledger = [0],
                                        conv_a ledger untouched at [0,1]
      (The TS oracle reaches the same result with ATTACH_TURN_BUDGET_CHARS=260;
       the Rust binary cannot set that env var per test because turn_budget() is
       process-cached, so the fixture width carries the budget instead.)
  turn::unrelated_followup_is_not_glued_onto_the_previous_topic_f07
      whale history + "and the cpu fan noise?" -> serves the CPU passage ONLY
      (no "whale" in the injected block), block lands directly before the user
      turn (msgs[2] system / msgs[3] user).
  turn::an_unanswerable_followup_still_falls_back_to_its_antecedent_f07
      "and in winter?" matched nothing raw -> the anchored fallback serves the
      whale-migration passage (the fix must not silence real follow-ups).
  turn::a_document_without_a_timeline_never_routes_to_a_time_window_f07
      "1:20 aspect ratio" document question still serves the passage and
      invents no [HH:MM:SS] header.
  turn::a_timeline_bearing_attachment_resolves_an_explicit_cue_f07
      durationSec + timed chunks: "at 5:30" -> window [150,510] carries the
      [00:01:40 - 00:03:10] header and excludes segment 0 (0-90).
  store::shown_ledger_v2_scopes_by_conversation_and_query_f07 (session 33a)
  store::shown_mutex_serializes_writers_and_never_loses_a_key_f07 (12 threads
      x 5 writes, every key present, lock dir never outlives a write)
  retrieve::comparative_windows_select_the_cues_not_the_hull_f07 (windows
      [(0,210),(360,720)] -> chunks [0,1,3,4,5]; positive control with the SAME
      from_sec/to_sec and no windows -> [0,1,2,3,4,5])

